{"ref":"BDB, עֲנָק","hw":"עֲנָק","html":"† I. <big><span dir=\"rtl\">עֲנָק</span></big>  <strong>n.</strong>[<strong>m.</strong>] <strong>neck</strong>, only in <strong>epith. gent.</strong> <span dir=\"rtl\">בְּנֵי הָעֲנָק</span> <em>long-necked</em> (tall) <em>men</em>, early giant people about Hebron and in Philistia, Ενακ, Εναχ, <a data-ref=\"Joshua 15:14\" href=\"/Joshua.15.14\">Jos 15:14</a> (JE) = <a data-ref=\"Judges 1:20\" href=\"/Judges.1.20\">Ju 1:20</a>, without art. <a data-ref=\"Numbers 13:33\" href=\"/Numbers.13.33\">Nu 13:33</a> (JE), <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 9:2\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.9.2\">Dt 9:2</a>; also <span dir=\"rtl\">יְלִידַי הָע׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Numbers 13:22\" href=\"/Numbers.13.22\">Nu 13:22</a>, <a data-ref=\"Numbers 13:28\" href=\"/Numbers.13.28\">28</a>; <a data-ref=\"Joshua 15:14\" href=\"/Joshua.15.14\">Jos 15:14</a> (all JE); called also <span dir=\"rtl\">עֲנָקִים</span> <em>long-necks</em>, Ενακειμ, <a data-ref=\"Joshua 14:12\" href=\"/Joshua.14.12\">Jos 14:12</a>, <a data-ref=\"Joshua 14:15\" href=\"/Joshua.14.15\">15</a> (JE), <a data-ref=\"Joshua 11:21\" href=\"/Joshua.11.21\">11:21</a>, <a data-ref=\"Joshua 11:22\" href=\"/Joshua.11.22\">22</a> (D), <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 2:10\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.2.10\">Dt 2:10</a>, <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 2:11\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.2.11\">11</a>, <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 2:21\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.2.21\">21</a> + <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 47:5\" href=\"/Jeremiah.47.5\">Je 47:5</a> (read <span dir=\"rtl\">עֲנָקִים</span> for MT <span dir=\"rtl\">עִמְקָם</span>), and perhaps <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 12:16\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.12.16\">1 Ch 12:16</a> (v. <a data-ref=\"BDB, עֵ֫מֶק\" href=\"/BDB,_עֵ֫מֶק\", dir=\"rtl\">עֵמֶק</a> <em>ad</em> fin.); <span dir=\"rtl\">בְּנֵי עֲנָקִים</span> <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 1:28\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.1.28\">1:28</a> (𝔊 γίγαντες, cf. <a data-ref=\"Numbers 13:33\" href=\"/Numbers.13.33\">Nu 13:33</a>), <a data-ref=\"Numbers 9:2\" href=\"/Numbers.9.2\">9:2</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">עֲנָק</span> later (erron.) as eponym. ancestor of Anaḳim <a data-ref=\"Joshua 15:13\" href=\"/Joshua.15.13\">Jos 15:13</a> = <span dir=\"rtl\">עֲנוֹק</span> <a data-ref=\"Joshua 21:11\" href=\"/Joshua.21.11\">21:11</a> (both P).—Vid. especially Mey<sup>ZAW i (1881), 139</sup> GFM <a data-ref=\"Judges 1:10\" href=\"/Judges.1.10\">Ju 1:10</a>, <a data-ref=\"Judges 1:20\" href=\"/Judges.1.20\">20</a> Che<sup>Ency. Bib. ANAK</sup>.","next":"BDB, עֲנָק²","prev":"BDB, ענק"}